cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite both the article and this repository as below."
type: software
title: "Which quantities of a bioenergetic digital twin of an athlete can be individualized? Identifiability of a two-compartment model of critical power - a simulation study"
abstract: "Source code, synthetic data, raw outputs and analysis scripts accompanying the manuscript on which quantities of a bioenergetic digital twin of an athlete can be individualized: structural and practical identifiability of a reduced two-compartment Margaria-Morton model, estimator efficiency against the Cramer-Rao bound (trust-region least squares, Differential Evolution, physics-informed network), out-of-sample prediction, departures from the generating model, and identifiability under oxygen uptake and time to exhaustion. Supersedes versions 1.0.0 and 2.0.0."
